From: TB378FC Porting Team <porting@tb378fc.local>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a6xx: synchronize non-coherent draws before coherent fbfetch

Regular 3D draws emit GRAS_SC_CNTL.SINGLE_PRIM_MODE = NO_FLUSH, whereas
coherent GL_EXT_shader_framebuffer_fetch draws emit FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP
(GMEM) or FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP_AND_OVERWRITE (SYSMEM). On Adreno 830 (a8xx),
FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP(_AND_OVERWRITE) only orders against prior primitives in
that mode and does not wait for or flush preceding NO_FLUSH draws still
in SP/RB or CCU, causing coherent fbfetch draws (e.g. Skia GaneshGL LCD
subpixel glyph quads over gradient buttons) to read stale pre-draw color.

Track whether non-coherent-fbfetch draws have been emitted in fd_batch
and emit FD6_FLUSH_CCU_COLOR | FD6_INVALIDATE_CACHE | FD6_WAIT_FOR_IDLE
when transitioning to a coherent fbfetch draw.

License: MIT
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_batch.h b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_batch.h
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_batch.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_batch.h
@@ -120,6 +120,11 @@
     */
    bool needs_wfi : 1;
 
+   /* Set when a draw that does not use coherent fbfetch (SINGLE_PRIM_MODE == NO_FLUSH)
+    * has been emitted in this batch; cleared once flushed before a coherent fbfetch draw.
+    */
+   bool has_non_coherent_fbfetch_draws : 1;
+
    /* To decide whether to render to system memory, keep track of the
     * number of draws, and whether any of them require multisample,
     * depth_test (or depth write), stencil_test, blending, and
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc
@@ -488,6 +488,21 @@
        DRAW == DRAW_INDIRECT_OP_INDIRECT_COUNT)
       ctx->batch->barrier |= FD6_WAIT_FOR_ME;
 
+   const bool coherent_fbfetch =
+      emit.fs->fs.uses_fbfetch_output &&
+      ((ctx->blend && ctx->blend->blend_coherent) ||
+       emit.fs->fs.fbfetch_coherent);
+   if (coherent_fbfetch) {
+      if (ctx->batch->has_non_coherent_fbfetch_draws) {
+         ctx->batch->barrier |= FD6_FLUSH_CCU_COLOR |
+                                FD6_INVALIDATE_CACHE |
+                                FD6_WAIT_FOR_IDLE;
+         ctx->batch->has_non_coherent_fbfetch_draws = false;
+      }
+   } else {
+      ctx->batch->has_non_coherent_fbfetch_draws = true;
+   }
+
    fd6_barrier_flush<CHIP>(cs, ctx->batch);
 
    if (is_indirect(DRAW)) {
